1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:03,258
Mmm…

2
00:00:03,308 --> 00:00:04,457
It smells like rain!

3
00:00:04,507 --> 00:00:06,794
That smell of wet earth after a shower.

4
00:00:06,844 --> 00:00:08,712
Yet tap water smells of nothing.

5
00:00:08,762 --> 00:00:11,280
So where does the smell of rain come from?

6
00:00:12,129 --> 00:00:14,189
Noah sniffs a glass of water: nothing.

7
00:00:14,239 --> 00:00:16,077
Mila sniffs a handful of wet soil:

8
00:00:16,127 --> 00:00:16,744
there it is!

9
00:00:16,794 --> 00:00:18,854
The smell doesn't come from the water…

10
00:00:18,904 --> 00:00:20,015
but from the ground.

11
00:00:20,782 --> 00:00:22,296
Discovery mission!

12
00:00:24,812 --> 00:00:25,417
Mini mode!

13
00:00:25,467 --> 00:00:28,628
In the soil live tiny bacteria that make a scent:

14
00:00:28,678 --> 00:00:29,152
geosmin.

15
00:00:29,202 --> 00:00:30,332
Plants, meanwhile,

16
00:00:30,382 --> 00:00:33,019
leave oils on the ground during dry days.

17
00:00:33,069 --> 00:00:35,428
The soil is full of sleeping scents.

18
00:00:36,204 --> 00:00:37,953
A drop falls on the soil:

19
00:00:38,003 --> 00:00:39,823
it traps tiny air bubbles.

20
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:41,550
The bubbles rise, burst,

21
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,421
and shoot out a tiny mist…

22
00:00:43,471 --> 00:00:44,837
loaded with scents!

23
00:00:45,611 --> 00:00:47,191
These scents fly up to your nose.

24
00:00:47,241 --> 00:00:48,573
And your nose is a champion:

25
00:00:48,623 --> 00:00:52,179
it can smell geosmin even when there's just one drop in a swimming pool!

26
00:00:53,642 --> 00:00:56,825
That's why the smell is stronger after days without rain:

27
00:00:56,875 --> 00:00:58,243
the scents have piled up.

28
00:00:58,293 --> 00:01:00,115
A gentle little rain, and whoosh,

29
00:01:00,165 --> 00:01:01,186
it all flies away.

30
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:04,021
That's why rain has a smell.

31
00:01:05,505 --> 00:01:07,262
The smell of rain comes from the soil:

32
00:01:07,312 --> 00:01:10,402
scents from bacteria and plants that the drops send into the air.

33
00:01:11,978 --> 00:01:14,029
With an adult, on a dry day:

34
00:01:14,079 --> 00:01:17,256
water a patch of soil, lean in and breathe.

35
00:01:17,306 --> 00:01:19,633
The smell of rain, made by you!

36
00:01:20,411 --> 00:01:22,311
And why do stars twinkle?

37
00:01:22,361 --> 00:01:23,921
The answer tomorrow.
